---
title: Butterscotch Pudding
description: Deep, slightly burnt butterscotch pudding, with the boiling caramel poured over the yolks instead of tempering them.
tags: [pudding]
course: dessert
source:
  name: Cook's Illustrated
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/7266-best-butterscotch-pudding
servings: 8
time: 3h50m
---

> When taking the temperature of the caramel, tilt the pan and move the thermometer back and forth to equalize hot and cool spots. Work quickly when pouring the caramel mixture over the egg mixture to ensure proper thickening.

> Serve the pudding with lightly sweetened whipped cream.

Bring the @unsalted butter{12%tbsp}(cut into 1/2-inch pieces), @granulated sugar{99%g}(3 1/2 oz, 1/2 cup), @dark brown sugar{99%g}(3 1/2 oz, 1/2 cup packed), @water{1/4%cup}, @light corn syrup{2%tbsp}, @lemon juice{1%tsp}, and @salt{3/4%tsp} to a boil in a large #saucepan{} over medium heat, stirring occasionally to dissolve the sugar and melt the butter.

Once the mixture is at a full rolling boil, cook, stirring occasionally, for ~boil{5%minutes}; the caramel will register about 240°F (115°C).

Immediately reduce the heat to medium-low and gently simmer, stirring frequently, until the mixture is the color of dark peanut butter, ~simmer{12-16%minutes} longer. The caramel should maintain a steady stream of lazy bubbles; if not, adjust the heat accordingly. It will register about 300°F (150°C) and should have a slight burnt smell.

Remove the pan from the heat; carefully pour @heavy cream{1/4%cup} into the caramel mixture and swirl to incorporate (the mixture will bubble and steam); let the bubbling subside. Whisk vigorously and scrape the corners of the pan until the mixture is completely smooth, at least ~whisk{30%seconds}.

Return the pan to medium heat and gradually whisk in the remaining @&heavy cream{3/4%cup} until smooth. Whisk in @whole milk{2%cup} until the mixture is smooth, making sure to scrape the corners and edges of the pan to remove any remaining bits of caramel.

Meanwhile, microwave the remaining @&whole milk{1/4%cup} until simmering, ~microwave{30-45%seconds}. Whisk the @large egg yolks{4} and @cornstarch{1/4%cup} together in a #large bowl{} until smooth. Gradually whisk in the hot milk until smooth; set aside (do not refrigerate).

Return the saucepan to medium-high heat and bring the mixture to a full rolling boil, whisking frequently. Once the mixture is boiling rapidly and beginning to climb toward the top of the pan, immediately pour it into the bowl with the yolk mixture in 1 motion (do not add gradually).

Whisk thoroughly for ~whisk{10-15%seconds} (the mixture will thicken after a few seconds). Whisk in the @vanilla extract{2%tsp} and @dark rum{1%tsp}.

Spray a piece of #parchment paper{} with vegetable oil spray and press it on the surface of the pudding. Refrigerate until cold and set, at least ~chill{3%hours}. Whisk the pudding until smooth before serving.
